 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery** (`docs/decisions/change-delivery-approach.md`). Committed revisions are pushed to browsers over self-hosted WebSocket sessions, accepting connection-capacity and reconnect/replay operational work in exchange for low-latency updates without recurring realtime-vendor fees or provider lock-in. Five-second HTTPS polling and a hosted realtime service were rejected.
